  "name": "Furry Connection North",
  "shortName": "FCN",
  "description": "Furry Connection North (FCN) was an annual furry convention in Michigan from 2008 to 2013, run by Furry Connection North Inc., a Michigan non-profit. It was first held in April 2008 at the Best Western Executive Plaza in Ann Arbor, and from 2009 at the Sheraton Detroit Novi. Created by 2 the Ranting Gryphon and the convention chair Gir to show furs a good time, it was especially party- and dance-oriented, with free beer for sponsors, alongside the usual dealers' room, artists' alley, fursuiting and panels. Attendance grew from the first edition to 1,259 in 2013, and the organizers announced in September 2013 that FCN would conclude after six years.",
